sarahmcdiarmid@nhs.net, ord=5], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0006, section=BMJ Open, kind=paragraph, page=1, bbox={l=146.9196, t=49.46990000000005, r=547.7596, b=225.45024867776692}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Manchester Intermittent and Daily diet Type 1 Diabetes App Study (MIDDAS-­ Type 1): protocol for a randomised feasibility trial of an intermittent and continuous low-­energy diet in patients with type 1 diabetes and overweight and obesity, ord=6], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0007, section=BMJ Open, kind=paragraph, page=1, bbox={l=146.9196, t=249.51669800000002, r=539.0669079999999, b=287.8394}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Sarah McDiarmid , 1 Michelle Harvie , 2 Azza Aglan , 3 Hannah Winterbottom , 1 Womba Mubita , 4 Amanda Hulme , 4 Jane Davies , 5 James Yates, 5 Suzanne Krizak, 5 Diane Perry, 6 Basil G Issa 4, ord=7], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0008, section=ABSTRACT, kind=paragraph, page=1, bbox={l=146.91959999999997, t=336.6478, r=340.60859999999997, b=476.5115081545064}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Introduction Rising levels of overweight and obesity among people with type 1 diabetes (T1D) contribute to insulin resistance, dyslipidaemia, retinopathy, cardiometabolic complications and psychological morbidity. Continuous low-­energy diets (CLED) providing approximately 800 kcal (3347 kJ)/day can produce significant weight loss in type 2 diabetes, and intermittent low-­energy diets (ILED) may be an alternative. The Manchester Intermittent and Daily diet Type 1 Diabetes App Study (MIDDAS-­Type 1) aims to assess the safety, acceptability and feasibility of remotely delivered ILED and CLED programmes for people with T1D and overweight and obesity., ord=8], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0009, section=ABSTRACT, kind=paragraph, page=1, bbox={l=146.9196, t=479.62179999999995, r=343.1104, b=707.4975081545064}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Methods and analysis Twelve participants with T1D and body mass index ≥27.5 kg/m 2 (≥25 kg/m 2 in high-­ risk ethnic minorities) recruited from an National Health Service (NHS) trust and research register in England will be randomised to a remotely delivered CLED (n=6) or ILED (n=6) for 12 weeks. The CLED includes a daily Optifast 850 kcal (3556 kJ) 75 g carbohydrate formula diet. The ILED includes 2 days/week of Optifast and 5 days of a portion-­ controlled Mediterranean diet (170-250 g carbohydrate/ day). Both groups will receive matched high-­frequency remote support from a dietitian, nurse and psychologist via telephone and/or the Oviva app. The primary outcome will assess safety (occurrence of severe hypoglycaemia, ketonaemia, ketoacidosis and time above and below target blood glucose). Secondary outcomes include study uptake, retention, dietary adherence, acceptability, intervention delivery fidelity and potential efficacy in relation to change in weight, insulin requirements, glycated haemoglobin, lipids, insulin resistance (estimated glucose disposal rate) and quality of life. Participants will be invited for optional repeat measurements at 52 weeks., ord=9], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0010, section=ABSTRACT, kind=paragraph, page=1, bbox={l=146.9212, t=710.6078, r=323.4706000000001, b=740.4915081545064}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Ethics and dissemination The trial protocol (V4.0/08.06.2022) was granted ethical approval by Cambridge East Research Ethics Committee (Ref: 21/, ord=10], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0011, section=STRENGTHS AND LIMITATIONS OF THIS STUDY, kind=title, page=1, bbox={l=364.8459, t=331.43390000000005, r=545.4938999999999, b=340.238166389178}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=STRENGTHS AND LIMITATIONS OF THIS STUDY, ord=11], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0012, section=STRENGTHS AND LIMITATIONS OF THIS STUDY, kind=list, page=1, bbox={l=364.8459, t=346.14790000000005, r=548.7729, b=376.03160815450644}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ This study addresses the unmet challenge of helping people with type 1 diabetes (T1D) and overweight and obesity lose weight safely., ord=12], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0013, section=STRENGTHS AND LIMITATIONS OF THIS STUDY, kind=list, page=1, bbox={l=364.8459, t=379.14790000000005, r=548.78136, b=409.03160815450644}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ To the best of our knowledge, this is the first study to trial continuous low-­energy diet among people with T1D and overweight and obesity., ord=13], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0014, section=STRENGTHS AND LIMITATIONS OF THIS STUDY, kind=list, page=1, bbox={l=364.8459, t=412.14790000000005, r=548.7990000000001, b=442.03160815450644}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ This study will add to the limited data on the safety and potential efficacy of intermittent low-­energy diets in people with T1D and overweight and obesity., ord=14], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0015, section=STRENGTHS AND LIMITATIONS OF THIS STUDY, kind=list, page=1, bbox={l=364.8459, t=445.14790000000005, r=548.79063, b=475.03160815450644}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Limitations include the small sample size, the diets are not isocaloric over the 12-­week trial period and the lack of control group., ord=15], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0016, section=STRENGTHS AND LIMITATIONS OF THIS STUDY, kind=paragraph, page=1, bbox={l=358.3452, t=503.8738, r=550.6031999999999, b=555.7896397502601}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=EE/0014). The study will inform progression to a full-­scale randomised controlled trial to test the efficacy of these programmes for patients with T1D and overweight and obesity.

Trial registration number NCT04674384; Pre-­results., ord=16], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0017, section=INTRODUCTION Background, kind=title, page=1, bbox={l=358.3452, t=576.1598, r=417.7552, b=596.964066389178}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=INTRODUCTION Background, ord=17], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0018, section=INTRODUCTION Background, kind=paragraph, page=1, bbox={l=358.3418, t=600.6998000000001, r=554.7852000000003, b=741.2812569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=There are approximately 400 000 people with type 1 diabetes (T1D) in the United Kingdom, with rates increasing by 4% annually. 1 T1D is associated with a healthy bodyweight; however, overweight and obesity is becoming increasingly common in this population due, in part, to modern more intensive approaches to manage hyperglycaemia with higher daily doses of insulin, as evidenced by the Diabetes Control and Complications Trial, and other studies. 2 3 The prevalence of obesity (body mass index (BMI) ≥30 kg/m 2 ), ord=18], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0019, section=INTRODUCTION Background, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=40.5, t=48.7201, r=291.00210000000004, b=264.19155695364236}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=in adults with T1D from the Pittsburgh Epidemiology of Diabetes Complications Study increased from 3.4% at baseline (1986-1988) to 22.7% (2004-2007). 4 This increase was greater in the group randomised to intensive therapy from 1% at baseline (1983-1989) to 31% in 2005. These increases were not associated with an ageing cohort and occurred faster than the general population. An Austrian health survey found 15 771 patients with T1D had comparable rates of overweight and obesity compared with the general population. 5 UK data from the Scottish Registry Linkage Study found rates of overweight and obesity in people with T1D from 2005 to 2007 were similar to the general population in women (27.5% and 27.6%, respectively) and lower in men (22.8% and 26.9%, respectively). 6 T1D and overweight and obesity contribute to insulin resistance, dyslipidaemia, non-­ alcoholic fatty liver disease, retinopathy, cardiometabolic complications and psychological morbidity. 7 8, ord=19], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0020, section=INTRODUCTION Background, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=40.5, t=267.78009999999995, r=288.39410000000004, b=349.38155695364253}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The nutritional management of type 2 diabetes (T2D) and overweight and obesity has been well researched. 9 In contrast, there is little research on weight management in T1D. Challenges in T1D include fear of hypoglycaemia and the burden of increased glucose monitoring and insulin adjustment alongside the energy restriction and increased physical activity required for weight loss., ord=20], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0021, section=INTRODUCTION Background, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=40.494699999999995, t=352.9701000000001, r=288.41409999999996, b=471.08155695364246}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Few randomised controlled trials (RCTs) have evaluated dietary approaches to assist weight loss in T1D. One 6-­month study (n=28) of modestly energy restricted (10%-20%) low-­fat or Mediterranean diets resulted in little weight loss, with non-­significant differences in BMI between the groups (-0.7 kg/m 2 and -1.1 kg/m 2 , respectively). 10 Modest weight loss (~2 kg) has also been reported in studies looking at the impact of low-­carbohydrate diets (50-130 g carbohydrate/day) on glycaemic control and cardiovascular risk factors in patients with T1D. 11 12, ord=21], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0022, section=Continuous and intermittent low-energy diets, kind=title, page=2, bbox={l=40.5, t=488.35010000000005, r=220.98800000000006, b=497.154366389178}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Continuous and intermittent low-energy diets, ord=22], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0023, section=Continuous and intermittent low-energy diets, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=40.5, t=501.0601, r=290.9919, b=692.1915569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Continuous and intermittent low-­energy diets (LED) are popular weight management diets which been widely studied and publicised for the management of T2D. Formula-­based continuous low-­energy diets (CLED) (800 kcal (3347 kJ)/day for 12-20 weeks) have been shown to achieve large weight loss and remission (≥10 kg weight loss in 81% of participants and 46% diabetes remission at 12-­month follow-­up). 13 Our Manchester Intermittent versus Daily Diet App Study (MIDDAS) RCT in people with T2D reported that a formula-­based intermittent low-­ energy diet (ILED) (820 kcal (3430 kJ) 2 days/week) for 28 weeks was as effective for weight and glycated haemoglobin (HbA1c) reduction as an isoenergetic formula-­ based CLED (820 kcal (3430 kJ)/day 7 days/week) for 8 weeks; however, diabetes medication reduction was greater in the CLED group. 14, ord=23], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0024, section=Continuous and intermittent low-energy diets, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=40.5, t=695.7801000000001, r=288.42079999999993, b=740.8715569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Patients with T1D attending our clinics have been asking for advice on ILED and CLED. However, there is currently little evidence of the safety or potential efficacy of these diets in patients with T1D., ord=24], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0025, section=Continuous and intermittent low-energy diets, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=306.89, t=48.720100000000116, r=554.8000000000002, b=189.3015569536425}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=A recent pilot randomised trial among patients with T1D and obesity (n=10) demonstrated the safety and feasibility of a formula ILED (600 kcal (2510 kJ) and 60 g carbohydrate/day for 2 consecutive days/week and eating to appetite on 5 days) and daily modest energy restriction (around 1500-2000 kcal (6276-8368 kJ) and 200-275 g carbohydrate/day) for 12 weeks. There were no adverse events (AEs) during the study, and rates of hypoglycaemia were unchanged from baseline. Body weight reduced (p<0.05) in both ILED median (IQR) -7.0% (IQR: -5.2%, -8.0%) and the daily dieting group -3.9% (IQR:-1.0%, -11.1%). 15, ord=25], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0026, section=Continuous and intermittent low-energy diets, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=306.8879, t=192.7201, r=554.7779, b=273.3015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The safety, acceptability, feasibility and efficacy of CLED (800 kcal (3347 kJ)/day) in T1D is not established. Patients with T1D may be at risk of diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA), a potentially life-­threatening condition as well as severe hypoglycaemia with a CLED. No studies have tested CLED compared with ILED in patients with overweight and obesity and T1D., ord=26], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0027, section=Remote multidisciplinary support, kind=title, page=2, bbox={l=306.88790000000006, t=289.7601, r=439.1458999999999, b=298.56436638917796}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Remote multidisciplinary support, ord=27], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0028, section=Remote multidisciplinary support, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=306.8861999999999, t=302.3001, r=554.7972000000002, b=478.87985695364245}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The Manchester Intermittent and Daily diet Type 1 Diabetes App Study (MIDDAS-­Type 1) will incorporate high-­frequency remote follow-­up by a multidisciplinary team (MDT) via telephone and/or the Oviva smartphone app which facilitates messaging, group interaction and self-­monitoring of weight, diet, blood pressure (BP) and physical activity. 16 High-­frequency remote follow-­up has been shown to enhance adherence, and to be equivalent to face-­to-­face care (matched for frequency), 17 or superior to low-­frequency face-­to-­face care in weight management interventions. 18 Remote follow-­up also reduces participant burden to attend face-­to-­face appointments. Participants will use the Freestyle Libre flash glucose monitoring system 19 so that the MDT can monitor glucose and ketones remotely., ord=28], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0029, section=Aims of this study, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=306.8863, t=507.8784, r=554.7959000000004, b=564.4598569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=MIDDAS-­Type 1 will assess the safety, acceptability and feasibility of remotely supported ILED (850 kcal (3556 kJ) and 75 g carbohydrate 2 days/week) and CLED (850 kcal (3556 kJ) and 75 g carbohydrate daily) programmes for 12 weeks in people with T1D and overweight and obesity., ord=29], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0030, section=Aims of this study, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=306.8963, t=567.8784, r=554.8155000000006, b=648.4598569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=If the feasibility trial achieves criterion on safety, recruitment, retention and adherence, then progression to a pilot RCT will be considered. This could inform the use of LEDs to help people with T1D and obesity lose weight, improve their metabolic status and reduce the risk of cardiovascular and other physical and mental comorbidities associated with T1D., ord=30], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0031, section=METHODS AND ANALYSIS, kind=title, page=2, bbox={l=306.8963, t=684.1484, r=406.34529999999995, b=692.9526663891779}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=METHODS AND ANALYSIS, ord=31], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0032, section=METHODS AND ANALYSIS, kind=paragraph, page=2, bbox={l=306.8963, t=696.6884, r=554.8057000000006, b=741.2698569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Standard Protocol Items: Recommendations for Intervention Trials (SPIRIT) and Template for Intervention Description and Replication (TIDieR) reporting guidelines were used. 20, ord=32], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0033, section=Design and setting, kind=paragraph, page=3, bbox={l=40.48999999999998, t=61.13009999999997, r=288.4159999999997, b=190.61155695364243}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=MIDDAS-­Type 1 is a randomised feasibility trial that will be performed in patients with T1D and overweight and obesity, recruited from an NHS hospital trust and NHS-­supported voluntary research register in England. Each participant will be enrolled for 14-16 weeks from randomisation to final follow-­up including a 2-­week 'run-­in' period and 12-­week intervention. Participants will be invited to attend trial visits at Manchester University NHS Foundation Trust (MFT), United Kingdom. Participants will receive follow-­up support from an MDT via telephone and/or the Oviva smartphone app., ord=33], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0034, section=Recruitment, kind=paragraph, page=3, bbox={l=40.49000000000001, t=220.51010000000008, r=288.37, b=241.18155695364248}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Potentially eligible participants will be recruited to the study via:, ord=34], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0035, section=Recruitment, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=40.49000000000001, t=244.69010000000003, r=288.40000000000003, b=265.36155695364243}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Poster displays or during routine clinical contacts at MFT., ord=35], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0036, section=Recruitment, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=40.49000000000001, t=268.8701, r=288.42109999999974, b=337.9015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=All patients with T1D (n=670) on the 'Help BEAT Diabetes' volunteer database (hosted by the NIHR Clinical Research Network for Greater Manchester: https://www.researchforthefuture.org/diabetes/) will be invited by post/email to check that they meet the eligibility criteria for the trial and to contact the trial team if they are interested., ord=36], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0037, section=Recruitment, kind=paragraph, page=3, bbox={l=40.49000000000001, t=341.41009999999994, r=288.39, b=374.1715569536423}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants will be provided with an information sheet about the trial to help them decide if they wish to take part., ord=37], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0038, section=Eligibility criteria, kind=title, page=3, bbox={l=40.49000000000001, t=391.4400999999999, r=107.99000000000001, b=400.24436638917786}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Eligibility criteria, ord=38], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0039, section=Eligibility criteria, kind=paragraph, page=3, bbox={l=40.49000000000001, t=404.07009999999985, r=237.68999999999997, b=412.65155695364246}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The eligibility criteria are presented in box 1., ord=39], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0040, section=Participant flow, kind=paragraph, page=3, bbox={l=40.48999999999998, t=442.5501, r=288.38950000000006, b=499.4915569536425}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participant flow through the study is outlined in figure 1. Informed consent will be obtained by a trial research nurse at the screening visit.

Provisionally eligible participants will commence a 2-­week 'run-­in' period, as described below:, ord=40], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0041, section=Participant flow, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=40.498, t=503.0002, r=288.4265999999998, b=572.0316569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants will follow their normal diet, but will sample the Optifast (Néstle Health Science, United Kingdom) meal replacement shakes to establish their preferred flavours and an appropriate bolus insulin dose per shake. Participants will be discouraged from undertaking a full low energy day until they start the diet., ord=41], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0042, section=Participant flow, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=40.498, t=575.5402, r=288.3947000000001, b=620.3916569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Key insulin adjustment principles will be reinforced in a remote group/1-1 education session with the diabetes specialist nurse (DSN) and diabetes dietitian., ord=42], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0043, section=Participant flow, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=40.498, t=623.9002, r=288.42439999999976, b=644.5716569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Trial the Oviva app used to communicate with the trial team (optional)., ord=43], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0044, section=Participant flow, kind=paragraph, page=3, bbox={l=40.5, t=648.0802, r=288.38, b=668.7516569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=At the end of the 'run-­in' period, the participant will attend their 'Baseline Visit':, ord=44], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0045, section=Participant flow, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=40.498, t=672.2602, r=288.4051999999998, b=705.0216569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The MDT will assess adherence with the trial protocol including capillary blood glucose and ketone testing, safe insulin adjustment and their suitability for the trial., ord=45], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0046, section=Participant flow, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=40.498, t=708.5302, r=288.3592999999999, b=729.2016569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Eligible participants will be randomised to ILED or CLED., ord=46], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0047, section=Box 1 Eligibility criteria, kind=title, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=54.5, r=412.5678999999997, b=63.30426638917788}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Box 1 Eligibility criteria, ord=47], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0048, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=88.07249999999999, r=500.4418999999998, b=96.12305445544553}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Willing and able to provide written informed consent., ord=48], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0049, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=99.07249999999999, r=439.4920999999999, b=107.12305445544553}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Male or female aged 18-70 years., ord=49], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0050, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=110.07249999999999, r=473.84419999999983, b=118.12305445544553}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Diagnosed with T1D for 12 months or longer., ord=50], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0051, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=121.07249999999999, r=549.1042699999999, b=129.12305445544553}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Multiple daily injection or continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion., ord=51], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0052, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=132.0725, r=488.5258999999998, b=140.12305445544553}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ HbA1c 48-108 mmol/mol (venous blood sample)., ord=52], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0053, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=141.18806199999995, r=550.9343, b=172.9562081545066}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ BMI ≥27.5 kg/m 2 and <50 kg/m 2 or ≥25 kg/m 2 and <50 kg/m 2 in high-­ risk minority ethnic groups, that is, South Asian, black African and African Caribbean., ord=53], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0054, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=174.18806199999995, r=548.7794099999999, b=194.95820815450656}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Completed Dose Adjustment For Normal Eating education 21 or equivalent structured education course for T1D., ord=54], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0055, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=196.18806199999995, r=499.42542000000003, b=206.12305445544553}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Access to a Freestyle Libre 2 handset and sensors. 19, ord=55], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0056, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=207.18806199999995, r=535.6869, b=217.12305445544553}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Access to and ability to use the Oviva app 16 and/or a telephone., ord=56], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0057, section=Inclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=220.0725, r=548.7811700000001, b=238.95820815450656}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Willing to be randomised to a formula-­based ILED or CLED (having tested the products)., ord=57], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0058, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=259.0725, r=549.0980599999996, b=277.95820815450656}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Evidence of severe hypoglycaemia in the last 12 months (more than one episode requiring third-­party assistance) or hypoglycaemia unawareness., ord=58], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0059, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=281.0725, r=513.8339, b=289.1230544554456}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Routine HbA1c ≥108 mmol/mol during the last 3 months., ord=59], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0060, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=292.07250000000005, r=548.7430999999996, b=310.95820815450645}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Unstable retinopathy, or grade R2 or later, or no retinopathy screen within last 12 months., ord=60], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0061, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=314.07250000000005, r=550.9318999999999, b=332.95820815450645}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Current treatment with weight loss medications Orlistat or a glucagon-­ like-­peptide-­1 or a sodium-­glucose cotransporter-­2 inhibitor., ord=61], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0062, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=336.07250000000005, r=409.09189999999984, b=344.1230544554456}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Diagnosed gastroparesis., ord=62], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0063, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=347.07250000000005, r=434.15509999999966, b=355.1230544554456}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Pregnant/considering pregnancy., ord=63], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0064, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=358.07250000000005, r=398.91109999999986, b=366.1230544554456}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Prior bariatric surgery., ord=64], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0065, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=369.07250000000005, r=500.36990000000003, b=377.1230544554456}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Unintentional weight loss ≥5 kg within last 6 months., ord=65], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0066, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=380.07250000000005, r=548.7628999999998, b=398.95820815450645}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Learning difficulties, lacking capacity or unable to understand English., ord=66], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0067, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=402.07250000000005, r=460.3829, b=410.1230544554456}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Known sensitivity to Optifast ingredients., ord=67], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0068, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=413.07250000000005, r=548.7938599999997, b=453.96020815450646}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Diagnosed eating disorder or severe binge eating or very low eating self-­efficacy as assessed by the following questionnaires: Binge Eating Scale 22 (score ≥27) and Weight Efficacy Lifestyle Questionnaire Short Form 23 (score ≤35)., ord=68], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0069, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=457.07250000000005, r=548.7872899999996, b=475.96020815450646}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Severe anxiety or depression as assessed by Generalised Anxiety Disorder Scale 24 (score ≥15) and Patient Health Questionnaire-­9 25 (score ≥15)., ord=69], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0070, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=479.07250000000005, r=548.7791899999996, b=497.96020815450646}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Hazardous or harmful drinking as indicated by Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test 26 (score ≥16)., ord=70], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0071, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=501.07250000000005, r=548.7963799999995, b=519.9582081545065}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Medications associated with weight gain, that is, lithium, antipsychotics or other psychotropic medications., ord=71], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0072, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=534.0725, r=459.98419999999976, b=542.1230544554455}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Current treatment with an anticoagulant., ord=72], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0073, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=545.0725, r=548.8044799999998, b=563.9602081545065}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Participants with severe loss of renal function (estimated glomerular filtration rate <30 mL/min/1.73 m 2 )., ord=73], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0074, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=567.0725, r=548.8034899999997, b=596.9562081545064}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Participants with psychiatric or physical comorbidity or scheduled for major surgery, which could compromise their safety or adherence to the study., ord=74], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0075, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=600.0725, r=542.6779999999997, b=608.1230544554455}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Current participation in other weight loss/diabetes research trials., ord=75], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0076, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=list, page=3, bbox={l=312.8879, t=611.0725, r=548.8052899999994, b=640.9562081545064}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=⇒ Unsafe use of the Freestyle Libre/insulin adjustment principles or inadequate capillary blood glucose and ketone testing during the 'run-­in' period., ord=76], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0077, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=paragraph, page=3, bbox={l=312.89089999999993, t=644.0665, r=548.7922399999995, b=662.9522081545065}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=BMI, body mass index; CLED, continuous low-­energy diet; HbA1c, glycated haemoglobin; ILED, intermittent low-­energy diet; T1D, type 1 diabetes., ord=77], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0078, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=caption, page=4, bbox={l=40.497100000000046, t=468.002362, r=554.3403999999999, b=531.7572}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Figure 1 Participant flow through the study. 1 Urine pregnancy test where required. 2 Body composition includes percentage body fat and fat-­free mass. ADDQoL, Audit of Diabetes Dependent Quality of Life; 35 AUDIT, Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test; 39 BES, Binge Eating Scale; 38 BMI, body mass index; BP, blood pressure; DSN, diabetes specialist nurse; eGDR, estimated glucose disposal rate; eGFR, estimated glomerular filtration rate; GAD-­7, Generalised Anxiety Disorder Scale; 30 HbA1c, glycated haemoglobin; PHQ-­9, Patient Health Questionnaire-­9; 31 S-­PAQ, Scottish Physical Activity Questionnaire; 36 WEL-­SF, Weight Efficacy Lifestyle Questionnaire Short Form. 29, ord=78], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0079, section=Exclusion criteria, kind=paragraph, page=4, bbox={l=40.49999999999994, t=559.3227, r=288.39, b=592.3841569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=All participants will be invited to attend follow-­up visits at MFT with a research nurse for a repeat of clinical measurements in weeks 4, 8 and 12., ord=79], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0080, section=Randomisation and blinding, kind=title, page=4, bbox={l=40.49999999999994, t=609.6527000000001, r=151.86999999999998, b=618.456966389178}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Randomisation and blinding, ord=80], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0081, section=Randomisation and blinding, kind=paragraph, page=4, bbox={l=40.499300000000005, t=622.4327000000001, r=288.4193000000003, b=667.7340569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Eligible participants will be randomised 1:1 to ILED or CLED using a sealed envelope process by the research dietitian. 21 No stratification will be used given the small sample size., ord=81], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0082, section=Randomisation and blinding, kind=paragraph, page=4, bbox={l=40.499300000000005, t=671.3926, r=288.41510000000005, b=741.1740569536423}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants and clinicians will not be blinded to the treatment allocation. Laboratory results will be assessed by blinded independent laboratory staff. Analysis and interpretation of the results will be conducted by a member of the research team independent of the intervention and blinded to group allocation., ord=82], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0083, section=Interventions, kind=paragraph, page=4, bbox={l=306.88929999999993, t=571.8525999999999, r=554.7683000000002, b=592.6440569536423}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Figure 1 includes a summary of the two dietary programmes., ord=83], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0084, section=CLED programme, kind=paragraph, page=4, bbox={l=306.88929999999993, t=622.6626, r=554.8102000000006, b=741.1340569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants will be asked to follow the Optifast LED 7 days/week for 12 weeks providing approximately 850 kcal (3556 kJ) and 75 g carbohydrate/day. The diet consists of three Optifast shakes/soups (216 kcal (904 kJ) and 19 g carbohydrate/sachet) plus 7×80 g portions of non-­starchy vegetables (approximately 120 kcal (502 kJ) and 18 g carbohydrate), one dessertspoon of oil (80 kcal (335 kJ)) and 2-2.5 L of calorie-­free fluids. Participants will be asked to avoid alcohol and excessive caffeine to minimise the risk of dehydration., ord=84], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0085, section=ILED programme, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=40.49549999999999, t=61.17010000000005, r=290.99, b=275.96155695364234}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants will be asked to follow the Optifast LED on 2 consecutive days/week plus 5 days of a portion-­ controlled Mediterranean diet to achieve at least a 25% energy restriction across the week. The maximum dietary intake allowed on each of the Mediterranean diet days will be, for example, 2200 kcal (9204 kJ)/day for a man and 1800 kcal (7531 kJ)/day for a woman aged 50 years old with a BMI of 35. The diet prescription on the Mediterranean days is personalised to each participant. The estimation is based on the Mifflin equation, 22 multiplied by participants' self-­reported physical activity levels. 23 The Mediterranean diet used described previously by Harvie et al 24 is relatively high in protein (25% energy) with moderate carbohydrate (45% energy from low glycaemic load wholegrain carbohydrates) and moderate fat (30% energy from fat: 15% monounsaturated, 8% polyunsaturated and 7% saturated fatty acids) and limits alcohol to <10 units/week., ord=85], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0086, section=ILED programme, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=40.5022, t=279.51009999999997, r=288.4036000000001, b=360.8715569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The Mediterranean diet described contains approximately 150-300 g carbohydrate/day depending on an individual's energy requirements. Energy-­controlled Mediterranean diets are considered optimum for reducing weight, BP and improving lipid profiles 25 26 and may reduce the incidence of cardiovascular disease in people with T1D. 27, ord=86], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0087, section=ILED programme, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=40.5, t=364.4201, r=290.99530000000004, b=470.04155695364244}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants in both groups who are unable to tolerate Optifast during the 12-­week intervention will be offered a food-­based LED with a similar macronutrient profile to Optifast. This will comprise 250 g of lean protein foods (eg, lean meat, fish, eggs and vegetarian proteins), five portions of non-­starchy vegetables, three portions of low-­ fat dairy (eg, 200 mL milk is one portion), one portion of unsaturated fat (eg, small handful nuts), one portion of fruit, and one carbohydrate portion (eg, slice of bread)., ord=87], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0088, section=Physical activity, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=40.5, t=499.9801, r=288.41440000000006, b=678.3815569536423}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants will be asked to maintain their current activity levels to simplify glucose management and to help isolate the effects of the diets on weight and HbA1c. However, participants will be advised to avoid vigorous activity until they are familiar with the effect of their allocated LED on blood glucose. Participants will be advised to use principles from their previous diabetes education course, for example, Dose Adjustment For Normal Eating (DAFNE) 28 on managing insulin with physical activity. They will be encouraged to plan physical activity so that they can adjust their insulin prior to physical activity rather than relying on additional carbohydrate. All participants will be encouraged to monitor their blood glucose before, during and after physical activity and carry hypoglycaemia treatment., ord=88], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0089, section=Behavioural support, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=40.504400000000004, t=48.720100000000116, r=554.7944, b=741.1615569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Both groups will receive matched frequency of behavioural support from an MDT including a diabetes specialist dietitian, DSN and psychologist (if eligible) (figure 1).

Participants will be invited to communicate with the MDT via the Oviva smartphone app. The app facilitates messaging, and self-­monitoring of weight, diet, BP and physical activity., ord=89], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0090, section=Behavioural support, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=306.8944, t=96.7201, r=554.8037000000003, b=141.30155695364238}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants will be invited to participate in group messaging with other participants in their allocated diet group. If participants choose not to use the app, then scheduled follow-­up will be done by telephone., ord=90], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0091, section=Behavioural support, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=306.89439999999996, t=144.7201, r=554.7853000000003, b=165.30155695364238}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The support provided by the MDT to both groups is detailed in the online supplemental table., ord=91], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0092, section=Behavioural support, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=306.8899, t=168.7201, r=554.8139, b=273.3015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The diabetes dietitian will provide education on the LEDs and how to use the Oviva app, either by telephone or face to face at the baseline visit. All participants will be provided with written support materials, including recipes and meal plans. The DSN will provide education on the Freestyle Libre 19 and the study requirements around self-­monitoring of blood glucose/ketones and medication adjustment face to face at the screening and baseline visits., ord=92], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0093, section=Behavioural support, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=306.88610000000006, t=276.7201, r=557.3748, b=429.30155695364243}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Enhanced psychology support from the trial psychologist will be available for participants with questionnaire scores indicating low self-­efficacy (score 36-45 on Weight Efficacy Lifestyle Questionnaire Short Form (WEL-­SF) 29 ), moderate anxiety (score 10-14 on Generalised Anxiety Disorder Scale (GAD-­7) 30 ) or moderate depression (score 10-14 on Patient Health Questionnaire-­9 (PHQ-­ 9) 31 ). GAD-­7 and PHQ-­9 will be repeated at the week 4 and 8 appointments to check the well-­being of participants while on the trial. Psychological intervention will be informed by cognitive-behavioural therapy, Motivational Interviewing and Acceptance and Commitment Therapy. 32, ord=93], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0094, section=Behavioural support, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=306.88789999999995, t=432.7201, r=554.7970000000006, b=549.3015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=All members of the MDT will be trained in motivational interviewing techniques (a well-­established model of supporting behavioural change with proven efficacy in facilitating weight loss), to support dietary behavioural changes. Both programmes will use behaviour change techniques such as problem solving and feedback on behaviour, identified as being effective at reducing HbA1c. 33 The programmes will also use established behaviour change techniques, such as goal setting and self-­monitoring. 34, ord=94], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0095, section=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, kind=title, page=5, bbox={l=306.8879, t=564.1701, r=495.6548999999997, b=572.9342201716738}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, ord=95], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0096, section=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=306.8879, t=576.7101, r=554.7969000000006, b=645.2915569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants will sign a treatment contract to adhere to flash and capillary glucose, ketone and BP monitoring plans (see online supplemental appendix) using the Libre, and a BP monitor provided by the study team. Glucose and ketone data will be visible to the study team on the LibreView website. 19, ord=96], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0097, section=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, kind=paragraph, page=5, bbox={l=306.8879, t=648.7101, r=554.8037000000006, b=717.2915569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participants will be asked to report their BP fortnightly and their weight weekly via the Oviva app and/or by telephone.

Participants will be advised to report promptly via telephone and/or the Oviva app if they experience any of the following:, ord=97], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0098, section=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, kind=list, page=5, bbox={l=306.8859, t=720.7101, r=554.7884000000004, b=741.2915569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Severe hypoglycaemia, that is, blood glucose <3.0 mmol/L or nocturnal hypoglycaemia, ord=98], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0099, section=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=55.99999999999997, t=48.7201, r=288.39070000000004, b=81.30155695364238}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=<3.0 mmol/L or hypoglycaemia requiring third-­party assistance. Participants will also be asked to record episodes of hypoglycaemia (<4.0 mmol/L) in a diary., ord=99], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0100, section=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=40.4979, t=84.7201, r=288.4, b=105.30155695364238}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Blood glucose >15.0 mmol/L on two consecutive occasions., ord=100], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0101, section=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=40.4979, t=108.32010000000002, r=270.73911, b=117.35079306930697}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Blood ketones (β-hydroxybutyrate) >1.0 mmol/L., ord=101], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0102, section=Self-monitoring of glucose, ketones, BP and weight, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=40.4979, t=120.7201, r=163.24999999999997, b=129.30155695364238}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Systolic BP >165 mm Hg., ord=102], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0103, section=Diabetes and antihypertensive medication management, kind=title, page=6, bbox={l=40.5, t=141.18010000000004, r=246.30599999999995, b=149.9442201716738}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Diabetes and antihypertensive medication management, ord=103], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0104, section=Diabetes and antihypertensive medication management, kind=paragraph, page=6, bbox={l=40.49619999999999, t=153.7201, r=288.4119999999999, b=366.30155695364243}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The trial diabetes and antihypertensive medication management plans are detailed in the online supplemental appendix. The diabetes medication management plan for multiple daily injection and continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion has been adapted from a protocol tested in a recent ILED trial of people with T1D 15 and DAFNE insulin dose adjustment principles. 28 When a participant commences their allocated diet, basal insulin will be reduced by 50% on low-­energy days, and 10% on Mediterranean days. Participants' existing insulin to carbohydrate ratios and sensitivity factors will continue. Participants on metformin will continue with their existing dose when they commence the trial. Insulin will be adjusted after baseline according to the diabetes medication management plan and clinical need. All changes to medications will be agreed with the trial doctor. General practitioners (GPs) will be notified by letter of the enrolment of their patients and changes to medications., ord=104], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0105, section=End of intervention, kind=paragraph, page=6, bbox={l=40.4962, t=390.7201, r=288.41700000000003, b=483.30155695364243}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=At week 12, participants' care will revert to their usual diabetes MDT. The trial dietitian will provide dietary advice to support their future weight loss plans but will advise against continuing a LED without the support of a medical team. The trial diabetes nurse will provide a final review of blood glucose and advise on appropriate medication adjustment. Participants' GPs and diabetes teams will be informed accordingly., ord=105], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0106, section=Overall aim, kind=paragraph, page=6, bbox={l=40.4962, t=519.7201, r=288.39019999999994, b=564.3015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=The aim of the feasibility trial is to assess the safety, acceptability and feasibility of remotely supported ILED and CLED programmes for 12 weeks in people with T1D and obesity., ord=106], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0107, section=Safety, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=40.4962, t=600.7201, r=288.3892, b=645.3015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Episodes of severe hypoglycaemia, that is, capillary blood glucose <3.0 mmol/L or requiring third-­party assistance or any episodes of nocturnal hypoglycaemia<3.0 mmol/L., ord=107], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0108, section=Safety, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=40.496200000000016, t=648.7201, r=288.39619999999996, b=681.3015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Time spent in target (3.9-10 mmol/L), below target (<3.9 mmol/L and<3.0 mmol/L) and above target (>10 mmol/L) on the Freestyle Libre over 12 weeks., ord=108], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0109, section=Safety, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=40.4962, t=684.7201, r=288.4166, b=741.3015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Episodes of DKA (as defined by MFT guidelines: ketonaemia >3.0 mmol/L or significant ketonuria (more than 2+ on standard urine sticks) and blood glucose >11.0 mmol/L or known diabetes mellitus (type 1 or 2) and bicarbonate (HCO3 - ) <15.0 mmol/L and/or, ord=109], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0110, section=Safety, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=318.8922, t=49.250099999999975, r=554.8020000000001, b=70.76155695364241}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=venous pH <7.3) and blood ketone β-hydroxybutyrate levels above 1.0 mmol/L., ord=110], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0111, section=Safety, kind=paragraph, page=6, bbox={l=306.89219999999995, t=74.71010000000001, r=554.7922000000003, b=108.35155695364233}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Occurrence of serious AEs deemed potentially related to the dietary programmes, that is, outcomes requiring hospitalisation., ord=111], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0112, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.89219999999995, t=138.69009999999992, r=554.7522000000006, b=159.80155695364238}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Trial uptake, that is, percentage of those invited who are eligible and interested to take part., ord=112], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0113, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=163.75009999999997, r=554.7719999999999, b=184.86155695364243}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Retention to ILED and CLED interventions and completion of 12-­week assessments., ord=113], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0114, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=188.81009999999992, r=548.2922000000005, b=197.3915569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Adherence to blood glucose and ketone monitoring., ord=114], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0115, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=201.3401, r=554.7922000000003, b=247.5115569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Participant adherence to ILED and CLED including self-­reported adherence to LED days, preference for face-­to-­face contact with the dietitian and preference for food-­based versus formula-­based low energy days., ord=115], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0116, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=251.4601, r=554.7812000000005, b=285.1015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Seven-­day food diaries will be analysed using Nutritics nutrition analysis software to estimate energy, fat, saturated fat, carbohydrate and protein intake., ord=116], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0117, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=289.05009999999993, r=554.7795000000003, b=310.16155695364245}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Patient evaluation of the dietary programmes using a questionnaire., ord=117], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0118, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=314.1101, r=554.7822000000004, b=360.28155695364245}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Fidelity of delivery of the dietary programmes by the MDT, that is, percentage of contacts achieved, time spent by the MDT, preference for face-­to-­face contact with the dietitian, and attendance at follow-­up visits., ord=118], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0119, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=364.2301, r=557.3929, b=385.34155695364245}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Uptake to and continued use of the Oviva app for self-­ monitoring and communication., ord=119], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0120, section=Secondary outcomes, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=389.2901, r=554.7927000000003, b=422.93155695364237}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Minor adverse effects which may be associated with the dietary programmes, for example, constipation and fatigue., ord=120], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0121, section=Changes to the following from baseline to 12 weeks in both groups, kind=title, page=6, bbox={l=306.89219999999995, t=435.3401, r=554.2001999999999, b=444.5638768240343}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Changes to the following from baseline to 12 weeks in both groups, ord=121], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0122, section=Changes to the following from baseline to 12 weeks in both groups, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.89219999999995, t=448.41009999999994, r=554.7922000000002, b=469.5215569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Weight, body fat, fat free mass (bioelectrical impedance Tanita MC980MA), waist and hip circumference., ord=122], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0123, section=Changes to the following from baseline to 12 weeks in both groups, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.89219999999995, t=473.47009999999995, r=526.2922000000004, b=482.05155695364243}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Doses of insulin and other diabetes medication., ord=123], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0124, section=Changes to the following from baseline to 12 weeks in both groups, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=486.0001, r=554.7908, b=544.7015569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=HbA1c, number of hypoglycaemic (capillary blood glucose <4.0 mmol/L) events, blood lipids and estimated glucose disposal rate (eGDR) as a measure of insulin resistant (see online supplemental appendix)., ord=124], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0125, section=Changes to the following from baseline to 12 weeks in both groups, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8922, t=546.3757, r=554.7859000000001, b=582.2929569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Quality of life, that is, self-­efficacy (WEL-­SF), 29 anxiety (GAD-­7), 30 depression (PHQ-­9) 31 and Audit of Diabetes-­Dependent Quality of Life (ADDQoL). 35, ord=125], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0126, section=Changes to the following from baseline to 12 weeks in both groups, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8879, t=586.2415000000001, r=554.7878, b=607.3529569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Physical activity (Scottish Physical Activity Questionnaire (S-­PAQ)). 36, ord=126], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0127, section=Changes to the following from baseline to 12 weeks in both groups, kind=list, page=6, bbox={l=306.8879, t=611.3015, r=436.88790000000023, b=619.8829569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Change in BP medications., ord=127], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0128, section=Exploratory outcomes, kind=title, page=6, bbox={l=306.8879, t=632.2915, r=386.9068999999999, b=641.0556201716738}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Exploratory outcomes, ord=128], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0129, section=Substudy, kind=paragraph, page=6, bbox={l=306.88789999999995, t=657.8915000000001, r=554.7879000000001, b=741.6529569536424}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=At their week 12 visit, participants will be invited to attend and consent to a follow-­up visit at MFT at 52 weeks. This will capture change in weight, body composition, waist and hip circumference, BP, HbA1c, eGDR, blood lipids and quality of life (WEL-­SF, 29 GAD-­7, 30 PHQ-­9 31 and ADDQoL 35 ) to assess the long-­term impact of LEDs on people with T1D and obesity., ord=129], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0130, section=Trial progression criterion, kind=title, page=7, bbox={l=40.5, t=48.50010000000009, r=142.95, b=57.30436638917797}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Trial progression criterion, ord=130], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0131, section=Trial progression criterion, kind=paragraph, page=7, bbox={l=40.5, t=61.580100000000016, r=288.4100000000001, b=95.24155695364232}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=If the feasibility trial meets the following criterion, then progression to a future efficacy trial/definitive RCT will be considered:, ord=131], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0132, section=Trial progression criterion, kind=list, page=7, bbox={l=40.498, t=98.80010000000004, r=288.387, b=120.32155695364236}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Safety: withdrawal of ≤25% of patients with severe hypoglycaemia requiring third party assistance., ord=132], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0133, section=Trial progression criterion, kind=list, page=7, bbox={l=40.498, t=124.28009999999995, r=288.389, b=145.40155695364228}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Recruitment: successful recruitment of 12 patients to the study., ord=133], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0134, section=Trial progression criterion, kind=list, page=7, bbox={l=40.498, t=148.9601, r=287.09000000000003, b=157.94155695364236}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Retention: ≥50%. Complete the 12-­week assessments., ord=134], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0135, section=Trial progression criterion, kind=list, page=7, bbox={l=306.886, t=48.7201, r=554.778, b=69.30155695364238}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Adherence: >50% of low energy days completed in both groups., ord=135], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0136, section=Measurements, kind=paragraph, page=7, bbox={l=306.888, t=93.7201, r=554.7870000000003, b=114.30155695364238}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Table 1 is a summary of the measurements collected at each scheduled visit., ord=136], PassageDto[id=E-0001-0137, section=Measurements, kind=table, page=7, bbox={l=40.34315248481699, t=198.41983516973687, r=555.1831610541632, b=662.5998752181584}, page_width=595.2760009765625, page_height=793.7009887695312, text=Table 1 Schedule of measurements*

